{"data": [{"author_id": "1010729338902175746", "conversation_id": "2117223529577914419", "created_at": "2026-11-02T17:35:23.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117309609908281659"], "id": "2117309609908281659", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 163, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@scaling01 Loopmaxxing as a serious training style might be the next open-weight race after raw scale. Curious which Chinese labs are actually closing the loop on verifiable rewards versus just more synthetic data.", "url": "https://x.com/XRPSeattle/status/2117309609908281659"}, {"author_id": "1998177833156476928", "conversation_id": "2117223529577914419", "created_at": "2026-11-02T16:05:08.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117286899207582202"], "id": "2117286899207582202", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 240, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@scaling01 Link to abstract for people who prefer HTML version: https://t.co/j1nj8OgOss", "url": "https://x.com/car_dan20741/status/2117286899207582202"}, {"author_id": "5717402", "conversation_id": "2117223529577914419", "created_at": "2026-11-02T15:28:29.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117277677107441775"], "id": "2117277677107441775", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 344, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@scaling01 Same. The top 15 open models in my #fuscore benchmark of open vs frontier models are already all Chinese. Loops will probably cause another shift.", "url": "https://x.com/furukama/status/2117277677107441775"}, {"author_id": "1457877768104939523", "conversation_id": "2117223529577914419", "created_at": "2026-11-02T15:18:02.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117275046943289798"], "id": "2117275046943289798", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 324, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@scaling01 loopmaxxing is going to be the word of the week, i can feel it", "url": "https://x.com/Amankaushik481/status/2117275046943289798"}, {"author_id": "1828410741063348224", "conversation_id": "2117223529577914419", "created_at": "2026-11-02T14:35:47.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117264413229236375"], "id": "2117264413229236375", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 170, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@scaling01 lr carrying over from the smallest model up to 8 loops is the part that matters to me. if you have to redo the sweep every time you change loop count, nobody tries loops at real scale, so this probably does more for the loopmaxxers than any new architecture trick", "url": "https://x.com/jj_kovacs/status/2117264413229236375"}, {"author_id": "991872400361836545", "conversation_id": "2117223529577914419", "created_at": "2026-11-02T14:02:22.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117256003356172646"], "id": "2117256003356172646", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 80, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@scaling01 Looped layers trade parameters for sequential compute, which suits teams that are memory-limited more than FLOP-limited. The open question is who ships it in a production model first, since per-token latency grows with every loop.", "url": "https://x.com/EthanLinAI/status/2117256003356172646"}, {"author_id": "1434927365734510592", "conversation_id": "2117223529577914419", "created_at": "2026-11-02T13:26:02.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117246858166980975"], "id": "2117246858166980975", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 78, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@scaling01 The catch is latency. Loops add depth without adding weights, but each pass still runs in sequence for every token. I'd guess small on-device models benefit first.", "url": "https://x.com/aniroblue/status/2117246858166980975"}, {"author_id": "1628145685", "conversation_id": "2117223529577914419", "created_at": "2026-11-02T13:18:16.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117244905202598121"], "id": "2117244905202598121", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 711, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@scaling01 is it gonna be the same learning rate when the loop transfers from 8 to 48?", "url": "https://x.com/Van0SS/status/2117244905202598121"}, {"author_id": "1301751781056151553", "conversation_id": "2117223529577914419", "created_at": "2026-11-02T13:15:25.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117244186135245059"], "id": "2117244186135245059", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 66, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@scaling01 loops buy depth without buying parameters. whoever is most compute-poor will push this hardest", "url": "https://x.com/lefeiren129/status/2117244186135245059"}, {"author_id": "1503335161584566272", "conversation_id": "2117223529577914419", "created_at": "2026-11-02T13:00:12.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117240358711308629"], "id": "2117240358711308629", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 5, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@scaling01 Everyone's reading this as cheaper models. It's smaller models. Loop one layer 4 times and you still pay for 4 passes, so memory drops but compute per token doesn't. Cheap to host, not cheap to run.", "url": "https://x.com/ReyBrando1/status/2117240358711308629"}, {"author_id": "109482207", "conversation_id": "2117223529577914419", "created_at": "2026-11-02T12:38:27.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117234884636766349"], "id": "2117234884636766349", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 374, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@scaling01 Already here. IQuest's \"Loop the Loopies!\" in July looped a 20B MoE twice and passed a compute-matched 30B-A3B baseline after roughly 600 billion pretraining tokens. Post-trained it's mixed so far against Qwen3-30B: ahead on AIME 2024, behind on MMLU.", "url": "https://x.com/benshanyoufeng/status/2117234884636766349"}, {"author_id": "1916169928018948096", "conversation_id": "2117223529577914419", "created_at": "2026-11-02T12:23:31.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117231125554962494"], "id": "2117231125554962494", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 366, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@scaling01 loopmaxxing is what a tight GPU budget looks like from outside", "url": "https://x.com/shawnsbuilds/status/2117231125554962494"}, {"author_id": "1730969855783018496", "conversation_id": "2117223529577914419", "created_at": "2026-11-02T12:09:42.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117227649689120983"], "id": "2117227649689120983", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 459, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@scaling01 bytedance figured out how to tune hyperparams once and loop forever.", "url": "https://x.com/shadowaguy/status/2117227649689120983"}, {"author_id": "70070174", "conversation_id": "2117223529577914419", "created_at": "2026-11-02T12:06:06.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117226744034082827"], "id": "2117226744034082827", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 415, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@scaling01 distinct layers take a drunk's walk and drift like √L. one layer looped N times keeps leaning the same way, so it drifts like N. hence 1/N, not 1/√N", "url": "https://x.com/indrajeet877/status/2117226744034082827"}, {"author_id": "1769809221153943552", "conversation_id": "2117223529577914419", "created_at": "2026-11-02T12:00:44.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117225393900179586"], "id": "2117225393900179586", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 282, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@scaling01 curious if looping the same layers ends up great for laptops since it's fewer weights, or just slower per token", "url": "https://x.com/harshit10sehgal/status/2117225393900179586"}, {"author_id": "1825243643529027584", "conversation_id": "2117223529577914419", "created_at": "2026-11-02T11:53:29.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117223569608339965"], "id": "2117223569608339965", "lang": "zxx", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 3, "impression_count": 2860, "like_count": 8, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "https://t.co/hiWbudx9JA", "url": "https://x.com/scaling01/status/2117223569608339965"}], "includes": {"users": [{"id": "1010729338902175746", "name": "Sloane Bennett", "username": "XRPSeattle"}, {"id": "1998177833156476928", "name": "Dani", "username": "car_dan20741"}, {"id": "5717402", "name": "Benedikt Koehler", "username": "furukama"}, {"id": "1457877768104939523", "name": "Aman | Dev Studio🍀", "username": "Amankaushik481"}, {"id": "1828410741063348224", "name": "John Kovacs", "username": "jj_kovacs"}, {"id": "991872400361836545", "name": "Ethan Lin", "username": "EthanLinAI"}, {"id": "1434927365734510592", "name": "Aniroblue", "username": "aniroblue"}, {"id": "1628145685", "name": "Van0SS", "username": "Van0SS"}, {"id": "1301751781056151553", "name": "小楽子", "username": "lefeiren129"}, {"id": "1503335161584566272", "name": "Rey Brando", "username": "ReyBrando1"}, {"id": "109482207", "name": "youfeng", "username": "benshanyoufeng"}, {"id": "1916169928018948096", "name": "Shawn", "username": "shawnsbuilds"}, {"id": "1730969855783018496", "name": "ShadowAguy", "username": "shadowaguy"}, {"id": "70070174", "name": "INDRAJEET YADAV", "username": "indrajeet877"}, {"id": "1769809221153943552", "name": "Harshit Sehgal", "username": "harshit10sehgal"}, {"id": "1825243643529027584", "name": "Lisan al Gaib", "username": "scaling01"}]}, "meta": {"newest_id": "2117309609908281659", "next_token": "b26v89c19zqg8o3juzlyi9btispy1tcz35wue38hdfam5", "oldest_id": "2117223569608339965", "result_count": 16}}